index 9aace6c..dff3152 100644
--- a/docs/pocketforge-a133-peripheral-stubs.md
+++ b/docs/pocketforge-a133-peripheral-stubs.md
@@ -38,26 +38,23 @@ reg range) found FOURTEEN more peripherals between there and userspace:
 | TCON-TOP | `tcon-top@6510000`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-tcon-top` | `0x06510000` (`0x1000`) | `drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_tcon_top.c`, `sun8i_tcon_top_probe()` | Display is DT-SKIP (replaced by the virtio-gpu graft) but the real DT still declares this pipeline enabled, so the DRM component framework still probes+binds it. Unconditional `writel()`s clearing two reset-default registers, no poll. |
 | SID/eFuse | `efuse@3006000`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-sid` | `0x03006000` (`0x1000`) | `drivers/nvmem/sunxi_sid.c`, `sunxi_sid_probe()` | Bulk-reads the register file via `__ioread32_copy()` into an nvmem cell; a straight copy loop, no readiness poll. |
 | DE2 display-clocks | `bus@6000000/clock@0`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-de2-clk` | `0x06000000` (`0x10000`) | `drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/*`, `ccu_div_recalc_rate()` | Child-probed under the DE2 bus container via `of_platform_populate()`. `clk_hw_register()`'s standard `recalc_rate` op does a plain `readl()`, no poll. |
-| R-domain pinctrl | `pinctrl@7022000`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-r-pinctrl` (`r_pio`) | `0x07022000` (`0x400`) | `drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c` (same driver as `&pio` above) | Same audit as the already-stubbed main pinctrl: unconditional read-modify-write, no poll. Also the gate for observing the AXP717 PMIC-absence path (its I2C pins route through `r_pio`). |
+| R-domain pinctrl | `pinctrl@7022000`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-r-pinctrl` (`r_pio`) | `0x07022000` (`0x400`) | `drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c` (same driver as `&pio` above) | Same audit as the already-stubbed main pinctrl: unconditional read-modify-write, no poll. Its I2C pins route the AXP717 bus through `r_pio`. |
 | PWM | `pwm@300a000`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-pwm` | `0x0300a000` (`0x400`) | `drivers/pwm/pwm-sun4i.c`, `sun8i_pwm_get_state()` (via `pwm-backlight`'s `devm_pwm_get()`) | Plain `readl()` of the channel's period/duty register, no poll. |
 | DE2 mixer0 | `bus@6000000/mixer@100000`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-de2-mixer-0` | `0x06100000` (`0x100000`) | `drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c`, `sun8i_mixer_bind()` | DRM component bind for the display-engine compositor (real DT still enables it; replaced functionally by virtio-gpu). Unconditional `regmap_write()` resetting layer/blend config, no poll. |
 | TCON-LCD0 | `lcd-controller@6511000`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-tcon-lcd` | `0x06511000` (`0x1000`) | `drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c`, `sun4i_tcon_bind()` | Same DRM-bind class as mixer0/tcon-top; unconditional `regmap_write()`, no poll. |
-| R-domain I2C0 | `i2c@7081400`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-i2c` (`r_i2c0`, the AXP717 PMIC bus) | `0x07081400` (`0x400`) | `drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mv64xxx.c`, `mv64xxx_i2c_hw_init()` | Unconditional `writel()`s (soft-reset, clock divider, address, control), no poll. **This is the AXP717 PMIC-absence graceful-degradation gate** -- see below. |
+| R-domain I2C0 | `i2c@7081400`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-i2c` (`r_i2c0`, the AXP717 PMIC bus) | `0x07081400` (`0x400`) | `drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mv64xxx.c` | Promoted from a stub to QEMU's `allwinner.i2c-sun6i` model for registers `0x00..0x23`, wired to SPI 113. Only the DT reservation's register-free `0x24..0x3ff` tail remains an inert stub. |
 | Thermal sensor | `thermal-sensor@5070400`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-ths` | `0x05070400` (`0x100`) | `drivers/thermal/sun8i_thermal.c`, `sun50i_h6_thermal_init()` | Unconditional `regmap_write()`, no poll. |
 | USB OTG/MUSB | `usb@5100000`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-musb` | `0x05100000` (`0x400`) | `drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c`, `sunxi_musb_init()` | USB is explicitly SKIP (the infra-113 D10 cost this machine exists to avoid paying) -- this stub backs the single unconditional `writeb()` at probe time ONLY, it does not model USB. |
 | USB PHY | `phy@5100400`, `allwinner,sun50i-a100-usb-phy` | `0x05100400`+`0x05101800`+`0x05200800` (`0x100` each: `phy_ctrl`, `pmu0`, `pmu1`) | `drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c`, `sun4i_usb_phy_init()` | Same USB-SKIP class. Plain `readl()`-modify-`writel()` on `REG_HCI_PHY_CTL`/SIDDQ bits, no poll. Three disjoint reg ranges per the DT. |
 | EHCI0/OHCI0/EHCI1/OHCI1 | `usb@5101000`, `usb@5101400`, `usb@5200000`, `usb@5200400` | `0x100` each | `drivers/usb/host/{ehci,ohci}-hcd.c` generic core | Same USB-SKIP class. Plain register init/reset writes; any hardware-completion wait uses the generic core's own bounded jiffies timeout (confirmed live: OHCI logs "USB HC reset timed out!" and fails its probe cleanly with `-1`, never hangs). |
 
-### Regulator-less/PMIC-absence graceful degradation -- CONFIRMED (Phase C)
+### R-I2C0 and AXP717 promotion
 
-With `r_i2c0` stubbed, the AXP717 PMIC driver (`axp20x-i2c`) binds at its DT
-slave address, logs `AXP20x variant AXP717 found`, then its actual register
-read/irq-chip-setup I2C transfer times out through `i2c-mv64xxx`'s own
-bounded jiffies timeout (~2s, `mv64xxx: I2C bus locked ... time_left: 0`) and
-fails cleanly with `-110` (`ETIMEDOUT`) -- `axp20x-i2c 0-0034: probe with
-driver axp20x-i2c failed with error -110`. No wedge, no hang: boot proceeds
-straight through to `Run /init as init process` seconds later. This is
-exactly the "warn-and-continue" graceful degradation the real, regulator-less
-hardware config exhibits (see `helper-core.dtsi`'s own comments on this),
-now independently reproduced under `-M pocketforge-a133`. Full transcript:
-`pocketforge-automation` `scripts/qemu-pocketforge-a133-ui-evidence/serial.txt`.
+The earlier stub-only diagnostic proved that MMC0 deferred on the real DT's
+CLDO3 regulator supplier. R-I2C0 is now a functional sun6i controller and an
+AXP717 slave is populated at the DT address `0x34`. The PMIC is deliberately a
+bounded software register bank: IRQ enable `0x40..0x44`, W1C IRQ status
+`0x48..0x4c`, regulator enable `0x80`, and regulator controls `0x83..0x9f`.
+Unmodelled registers read zero and ignore writes. Stored regulator values are
+guest-programmed state, not hardware measurements; the model generates no
+PMIC events and exposes no interrupt output.
